{"id": "5b9ae12f4140fa6ebd4179c6", "name": "APT10 Targeting Japanese Corporations Using Updated TTPs", "description": "In July 2018, FireEye devices detected and blocked what appears to be APT10 (Menupass) activity targeting the Japanese media sector. APT10 is a Chinese cyber espionage group that FireEye has tracked since 2009, and they have a history of targeting Japanese entities.\n\nIn this campaign, the group sent spear phishing emails containing malicious documents that led to the installation of the UPPERCUT backdoor. This backdoor is well-known in the security community as ANEL, and it used to come in beta or RC (release candidate) until recently. Part of this blog post will discuss the updates and differences we have observed across multiple versions of this backdoor.", "author_name": "AlienVault", "modified": "2018-10-19T08:34:14.941000", "created": "2018-09-13T22:14:07.023000", "tags": ["APT10", "malware", "japan", "UPPERCUT", "office"], "references": ["https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2018/09/apt10-targeting-japanese-corporations-using-updated-ttps.html"], "public": 1, "adversary": "APT10", "targeted_countries": ["Japan"], "malware_families": [], "attack_ids": [], "industries": [], "TLP": "white", "indicators": [{"id": 1513533197, "indicator": "eservake.jetos.com", "type": "hostname", "created": "2018-09-13T22:14:08", "content": "", "title": "", "description": "", "expiration": null, "is_active": 1}, {"id": 1513533198, "indicator": "4f83c01e8f7507d23c67ab085bf79e97", "type": "FileHash-MD5", "created": "2018-09-13T22:14:08", "content": "", "title": "", "description": "", "expiration": null, "is_active": 1}, {"id": 1513533199, "indicator": "cca227f70a64e1e7fcf5bccdc6cc25dd", "type": "FileHash-MD5", "created": "2018-09-13T22:14:08", "content": "", "title": "", "description": "", "expiration": null, "is_active": 1}, {"id": 1513533200, "indicator": "f188936d2c8423cf064d6b8160769f21", "type": "FileHash-MD5", "created": "2018-09-13T22:14:08", "conten